From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:59:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] venus: tear down an object the context refused by its id

A guest names each object it creates by an id of its own choosing, and the
context refuses an id that another object already holds: it ends the
context and leaves the object out of its table. The creator has already made
the object and tracks it in its device, command pool or descriptor pool,
which later removes every tracked object from the table by id. The id finds
the object that holds it, so removing the refused one freed the original,
which its owner still tracked. Tearing the context down then walked a freed
list entry, and the host process died.

An object is now freed by the removal only when the table holds that object
under its id. One the table refused is freed where it is removed from its
owner, which was the only thing left undone for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/venus/vkr_context.h | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_context.h b/src/venus/vkr_context.h
index 3974ea49eb80c49884576576967e18ba822281fb..3cc586f41bf9292d7b47238638f68654b0b52614 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_context.h
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_context.h
@@ -258,9 +258,20 @@ vkr_context_add_object(struct vkr_context *ctx, struct vkr_object *obj)
 static inline void
 vkr_context_remove_object_locked(struct vkr_context *ctx, struct vkr_object *obj)
 {
-   assert(_mesa_hash_table_search(ctx->object_table, &obj->id));
-
    struct hash_entry *entry = _mesa_hash_table_search(ctx->object_table, &obj->id);
+
+   /* An object the table refused, because the guest chose an id that another
+    * object holds, was never entered under that id, though its creator still
+    * tracks it and removes it with the rest.  The id then finds the object
+    * that holds it, and removing that one frees an object that is still
+    * tracked.  Free only what the table holds; what it refused is freed
+    * here. */
+   if (unlikely(entry && entry->data != obj)) {
+      free(obj);
+      return;
+   }
+
+   assert(entry);
    if (likely(entry)) {
       vkr_context_free_object(entry);
       _mesa_hash_table_remove(ctx->object_table, entry);
